<div class="bb-quote"><b>JimmytheRat wrote:</b><br /><blockquote class="bb-quote-body">As far as I&#39;m concerned, this is like Nightmist being unable to redirect damage if she&#39;s immune to damage.&nbsp; If you consider the in-the-rulebook-this-is-what-happens-when-a-character-is-destroyed effect to be simultaneous with all other destruction effects, it opens up a very deep and very nasty rabbit hole.&nbsp; For example:Skydeck is in play.A hero is reduced to 0 hp.If you apply the OoO ruling here, you could place your character card on the bottom of your deck instead of being incapacitated.&nbsp; How would the game function then?
&nbsp;
</blockquote></div>
No no. This is exactly what I am saying is NOT the case. Being destroying <em>and</em> flipping to the incap side are <em>not</em> <strong>2 </strong>different effects happening <em>simultaneously</em>. Therefore the OoO ruling has no bearing at all in anyway in this case.Character cards, when their HP is reduced to 0 or below, flip instead of being destroyed. Thats always been the intent. Wrathful Gaze and similar effects are *exeptions* to the general rule of thumb not the other way around.

[/quote]
If that&#39;s the intent, the current wording does not reflect that. &nbsp;The current wording changes the effect of destruction, but doesn&#39;t replace the destruction.

&nbsp;

Incidentally, I believe you mean&nbsp;<strong>Hero</strong> character cards, as Villian characters flip whenever they say they do.
